<article class="env-proposition" id="0ELC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ELC">Proposition <span data-tag="0ELC">58.27.1</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ be a proper scheme over $k$. Let $\mathcal{L}$ be an ample invertible $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Let $s \in \Gamma (X, \mathcal{L})$. Let $Y = Z(s)$ be the zero scheme of $s$. Assume that for all $x \in X \setminus Y$ we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{depth}(\mathcal{O}_{X, x}) + \dim (\overline{\{ x\} }) > 1  \]
</div>
  <p> Then the restriction functor $\textit{FÉt}_ X \to \textit{FÉt}_ Y$ is fully faithful. In fact, for any open subscheme $V \subset X$ containing $Y$ the restriction functor $\textit{FÉt}_ V \to \textit{FÉt}_ Y$ is fully faithful. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The first statement is a formal consequence of Lemma <a href="/tag/0EJZ" data-tag="0EJZ">58.17.6</a> and Algebraic and Formal Geometry, Proposition <a href="/tag/0EL1" data-tag="0EL1">52.28.1</a>. The second statement follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0EJZ" data-tag="0EJZ">58.17.6</a> and Algebraic and Formal Geometry, Lemma <a href="/tag/0EL2" data-tag="0EL2">52.28.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>